     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n**The issue:** 1600 mg four times daily comes to **6,400 mg/day**.\n- The usual maximum single oral dose of ibuprofen is **800 mg**. This order is twice that.\n- The usual maximum daily dose for adults on prescription is **3,200 mg/day**. This order is twice that.\n- At these doses the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and heart problems go up a lot, especially in a 70-year-old.\n\n**Did you mean one of these?**\n1. **400 mg four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total). This may be what you meant if 1600 was the daily total.\n2. **800 mg three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n3. **800 mg four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n4. Something else\n\nTell me which one and I'll enter it right away. If you do mean 1600 mg per dose four times daily, please confirm that and tell me the reason. I'd then enter it with a note saying the dose is above the usual maximum and was confirmed by the attending, so pharmacy can see it when they verify the order."
      }
     ],
