      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I entered the order as written, after your confirmation. **The order ID is ORD-0001.**\n\n**What's on the order:**\n- Ibuprofen 1600 mg by mouth, four times daily (6,400 mg/day)\n- A dose alert note. It says the dose is twice the usual maximum single dose and twice the usual maximum daily dose, and that you confirmed it as written. It also says no clinical reason was given, so pharmacy may contact you before dispensing.\n\n**Things to consider at this dose:**\n- **Stomach protection:** consider a PPI to lower the risk of GI bleeding.\n- **Kidney monitoring:** check creatinine and urine output, especially at age 70.\n- **Blood pressure and fluid status:** watch for fluid retention and other heart effects.\n- **Drug interactions:** check for anticoagulants, antiplatelets, ACE inhibitors or ARBs, diuretics, and SSRIs.\n\nIf 1600 mg was meant to be the daily total, I can cancel this order and enter the corrected one."
      }
